WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.734
-Good evening.

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.768
I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:04.237
We hope you're
doing well tonight.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.138
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.540
Democratic senator
Raphael Warnock

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.043
is projected to defeat

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.011
Republican candidate
Herschel Walker

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.646
in the Georgia Senate
runoff race.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.681
And if you think
you're relieved,

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:19.218
imagine how relieved
Herschel Walker is.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:23.288
He just narrowly avoided
a six-year-long pop quiz

00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:25.191
he did not study for.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.292
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.161
That's right,
CNN last night projected

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.395
that Georgia senator
Raphael Warnock

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.930
will win reelection.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.634
And then Herschel Walker picked
up an iron to call and concede.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.536
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.775
The Trump Organization
was found guilty yesterday

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.910
in a New York court
for criminal tax fraud.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.547
Trump will be sentenced
to four years as president.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.482
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.517
That's right,
a Manhattan jury yesterday

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.219
found former President Trump's
company guilty

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.924
of orchestrating a 15-year
criminal tax fraud scheme.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.393
Though it succeeded -- Though --

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.528
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:05.464
Always something wrong
with the syntax of the joke.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:08.667
For me.
It was written fine.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.904
Let's do it one more time.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.204
Sorry, Baze.

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.406
You know what
the worst thing is?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.209
Our head writer
is allowed to fire me.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.078
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.647
That's right,
a Manhattan jury yesterday

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.582
found former President Trump's
company guilty

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.685
of orchestrating a 15-year
criminal tax fraud scheme.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.120
Though it succeeded for --

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.122
[Bleep]

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.124
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.126
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.130
No. How dare you?!

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.466
My name's on the door!

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.435
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.973
I'm going to try.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.042
Alright.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.510
"Though it succeeded
for so long..."

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.744
Okay.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.413
[ Clears throat ]

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:55.981
"Though it..."

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:59.485
"Though it succeeded for..."
Okay.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.722
"Though it succeeded..."
Okay.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.223
This better work.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.659
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.494
That's right,
a Manhattan jury yesterday

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.529
found former President Trump's
company guilty

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.333
of orchestrating a 15-year
criminal tax fraud scheme.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.068
Though it succeeded for so long,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.904
there's no way Trump
had anything to do with it.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.106
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.208
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.989
We got to have a rehearsal
from now on.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.024
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.029
President Biden
visited Arizona yesterday

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.597
for the first time
in his presidency.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:48.468
Said Biden, "Wow, the last time
I was here, this was all flat."

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.102
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.637
Alright, Baze, you know what?

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.338
I'm going to turn the tables.

00:02:53.338 --> 00:02:54.874
That joke makes
no [bleep] sense.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.275
Can you go back?

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.676
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.676 --> 00:03:00.613
Yeah, they all laughed
'cause he's an old man, ha-ha.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.714
But...

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.017
President Biden
visited Arizona yesterday

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.551
for the first time
in his presidency.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.953
So, like, for the first time
in two years.

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:10.923
That meant three years ago,
he was probably there.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:12.759
Why was it flat then?

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.927
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:18.330
Maybe if it was like "for the
first time since he was a kid,"

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.333
then the joke works.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.869
'Cause he's so old.
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.671
I just want to make something
clear to all of you.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:27.306
We're all doing a bad job.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.441
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.475
Okay?

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.381 --> 00:03:39.919
And I will make this same speech
at the Christmas party!

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.388
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.624
During last week's
White House state dinner,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.192
French president Emmanuel Macron

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.995
reportedly toasted to President
Biden's reelection campaign.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.297
Either that or Biden said
he was running again

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.965
and Macron
just started drinking.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.836
President Biden yesterday
encouraged Americans

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.638
to get updated
coronavirus vaccine shots

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:00.973
ahead of the holidays,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:05.077
if for no other reason
than Santa's 2,000 years old.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.880
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.515
Is that Scol?
Who wrote that?

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.784
Scollins?
Scollins wrote that joke.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.353
He's one of our writers
who doesn't like people.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:20.425
And what he wanted in the key
was Santa on a ventilator.

00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:23.396
[ Laughter, groaning ]

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.098
That's just hearing it.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:28.067
That's the reaction you make
when you hear it.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.203
He wanted to show it to you.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.304
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:35.741
New York's annual SantaCon
bar crawl is this weekend,

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:38.444
and more than 60 bars
are expected to participate,

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.780
as well as several local jails.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.648
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.384
BuzzFeed announced plans
yesterday

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.519
to lay off roughly 180 staffers.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.921
Even worse,
the way they announced it.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.857
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:59.465
Oy, somebody put Santa on
a ventilator with that joke.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.499
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.201
Ben &amp; Jerry's
announced yesterday

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.003
they will release a new flavor

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.005
curated by director
Ava DuVernay.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.307
Meanwhile, the
James Cameron-inspired flavor

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:11.577
is currently 10 years behind
and $200 million over budget.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.512
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.381
Regulators in Minnesota
this week

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.316
accused
a marijuana edibles company

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:20.152
of selling gummy bears that were
50 times more powerful

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.455
than what is legally
allowed to be sold.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.990
This actually happened
last year,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.425
but all the witnesses
just woke up.

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:29.328
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.831
And finally,
according to a new survey,

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:35.868
just 2% of Americans said
that they never felt happy

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.303
when someone they like
succeeds at something.

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:39.805
Or as they put it on Instagram,

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.141
"Oh, my God,
I love that for you."

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.309
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:46.079
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

